From 2c35d3554d5044e480e41c2907c0a11ebe816478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julia Klee <71413974+kleeedolinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:22:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] sendshortcut: keys resolve without held modifiers; the tap
 restores the real modifiers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Shift held (⇧⌘Z) made `z` unresolvable, a Cyrillic layout had no `c`, and every
tap sent all-zero modifiers afterwards: the app lost Caps Lock, the active layout
and the held Super until the next real modifier change. Policy in WolosKeys.hpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
